     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 2,400 mg per dose four times daily is 9,600 mg/day. That's well into the range where serious toxicity is expected (GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, CNS effects), and I don't know of any indication that justifies it. Normal kidney and liver function wouldn't make it safe. A single 2,400 mg dose is already around the maximum daily dose for many patients.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum), with a note on the indication and planned duration\n\nIf you need more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect than these give, I can enter a multimodal regimen instead, such as scheduled acetaminophen plus ibuprofen. A pharmacist consult may also help. If you think this dose is truly intended, it would need to go through your institution's pharmacy review or a direct order-override process, not through me.\n\nWhich would you like me to enter?"
      }
